invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_parser_ee.c
catches: handshake_strict_webpki
reason: the ALPN arm stops checking that the ProtocolNameList length
  counts the one name it holds, so a server may claim a list longer or
  shorter than the bytes it sent and still be accepted. RFC 7301 §3.2
  fixes that list at exactly one ProtocolName, and RFC 9846 §6 makes a
  length that does not fit a decode_error.
  bin/handshake_strict_webpki's claimed-length row objects.

--- old
    if (e.err || name_len == 0 || list_len != 1 + name_len || rb_left(&e) != 0) {
--- new
    if (e.err || name_len == 0 || list_len < name_len || rb_left(&e) != 0) {
